                <syl /><neume facs="#m-c120742d-be10-470c-944a-173e3eb2c9ae" type="punctum" xml:id="m-e8363a8d-8c74-4398-bf9d-560d373846eb">
                  <nc xml:id="m-720dc7a5-1266-42ad-9d69-d0600dca1360" pname="a" oct="3" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-9ca000a6-e579-4f7d-ba8b-d3fd82d61ae8">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-bee38bf4-1b4a-4012-ba9a-d36e3c45e6a4" type="punctum" xml:id="m-d5338fb9-84b8-405d-be64-e07b54c00a32">
                  <nc xml:id="m-5993dfd5-b129-4fa6-a034-3cc40181dc0d" pname="f" oct="3" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-7873a3ca-41ef-4a0a-8ff2-c77d5170cc1c">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-66708f81-8dea-41af-9c5d-254361478125" type="podatus" xml:id="m-30a81c47-216f-4f5c-9d68-cceb7b69d73c">
                  <nc xml:id="m-f10ea802-13ef-4d89-adde-1c7a27322e20" pname="g" oct="3" /><nc xml:id="m-29e7d0d6-5d79-4f45-9911-d90decaee684" pname="a" oct="3" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-c2db9bd7-1049-4cf9-ae54-0a3fa34675a2">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-de07ae22-31e9-46f3-b9e7-c1180cb233be" type="punctum" xml:id="m-6632d709-6a03-4317-a9aa-24d04fb3fcce">
                  <nc xml:id="m-3fd5d6d1-c27e-46c0-a865-a8961f630db1" pname="g" oct="3" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-463c1587-9323-4675-8b71-a28cc8c677c1">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-1b6c5cf2-27bb-497e-b650-ea507c73eb32" type="punctum" xml:id="m-9429f3df-58ca-465c-9d94-c0d0b2d4a48d">
                  <nc xml:id="m-9a17d5c2-a49f-4c3e-a8a1-6625f7acb36c" pname="f" oct="3">
                    <signifLet xml:id="m-823a9999-da71-4a19-81b9-8a5e92ddc6d0" /></nc></neume></syllable><divLine xml:id="m-d21d4955-a328-41c5-a227-6e3e01df04b2" facs="#m-1f03eb2f-4552-49bd-810b-7c708d50200c" form="maxima" /><divLine xml:id="m-fcd5039c-0f2d-40d9-8e53-29fff2dd200c" facs="#m-00a5cbe7-d4d3-48df-9848-2326f51b3554" form="maxima" /></layer></staff><div xml:id="m-428a3da4-55a8-4d84-8187-233ec2fadc9a"><lg xml:id="m-512da2dc-448e-4725-a0a2-8757167384e5"><l xml:id="m-47e43287-27d4-4c16-af8b-4aecf273964f" facs="#m-4f6a4d91-6079-4cdc-bd6e-bb5f1e04f913" label="ambiguous">1732</l><l xml:id="m-c0e8e512-3861-4abe-ad0e-40c7f7ca4558" facs="#m-c7c3b190-de42-488e-bd48-21e7ad1fe7d2" label="ambiguous">November 2.</l><l xml:id="m-017e7685-b9f0-4a22-9a42-ae58392455ec" facs="#m-f95b47b3-e9db-4541-9bc5-d3aaed3684f4" label="text-like">At Magn.8</l><l xml:id="m-629d289b-924d-40b2-a75a-3fa4a8d5e028" facs="#m-13ff92bf-4d08-4a40-9401-48b782d931c0" label="ambiguous">Ant. G. F</l><l xml:id="m-94cec1f9-b07c-4b25-9d26-90367b5c17e0" facs="#m-eff7653f-b61b-4496-91bd-ad978214ce9b" label="ambiguous">0</l><l xml:id="m-1b2644b8-89a6-46cc-90e7-4331563f4e1c" facs="#m-92b42b9f-5974-4417-9801-f04117005305" label="lyrics-like">quam glo-ri-ó-sum est régnum,* in quo cum</l><l xml:id="m-80d5dd03-902c-49d7-bce7-980d85de564e" facs="#m-1ae43359-1735-42eb-a5c8-1e627ba3d615" label="lyrics-like">amícti stó-lis ál-bis,</l><l xml:id="m-e8dabd11-0da2-454f-a5fe-f4ee622931ad" facs="#m-4e230ae7-ebab-4025-acfb-2d540dba860b" label="lyrics-like">Chrí-sto gáudent ómnes Sáncti!</l><l xml:id="m-0b839667-7eab-4773-9990-41c9ad050bd3" facs="#m-e64e4d24-10aa-43dc-94db-626994e77545" label="lyrics-like">se-quúntur A-gnum quo-cúmque í-e-rit. Eu ou a e.</l><l xml:id="m-e2b71d6d-0489-4177-87f3-2a321c86f81e" facs="#m-af4cd0a0-601a-49a7-bfe1-04bbd9bfd7a8" label="lyrics-like">Cant. Magníficat. 6. F. p. 211 or p. 213. — Prayer. Omnípotens. p. 1725.</l><l xml:id="m-3cef8518-f51d-493d-b89c-250eddd16221" facs="#m-e35cc6a0-dd17-44b8-a24a-aa238e01331e" label="text-like">2. Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed.</l><l xml:id="m-11a00f71-4521-4e72-86c0-37a5da7c4a86" facs="#m-a0138a23-3333-4bc8-ae7c-d4da83c75baf" label="ambiguous">Double.</l><l xml:id="m-67516429-1221-440d-8dd8-4121bd33e532" facs="#m-cc9d9307-143d-427b-b616-e545b6f55666" label="text-like">The Antiphons are doubled at Matins, at Lauds and at Vespers.</l><l xml:id="m-02a0f7ef-6348-4f4f-938d-9b84bff4bd5d" facs="#m-753bf616-d0be-4b71-8ef9-10b6ad6d010d" label="text-like">AT MATINS.</l><l xml:id="m-a0f23abc-067d-423f-88ab-487c702ce1e4" facs="#m-33755a06-0287-4f85-a857-e4662d48a1ad" label="lyrics-like">The Office begins directly by the Invitatory Régem cui ómnia vivunt. p. 1779.</l><l xml:id="m-bda42851-55fe-4d56-9b1c-9ed18fb6abad" facs="#m-5c11cc2e-48fd-4f88-882c-afacae37edf1" label="text-like">The Antiphons, the Psalms, and the Versicles of the three Nocturns are</l><l xml:id="m-9e5618e8-e06c-4323-8bd9-1e09d4f31164" facs="#m-af0a5317-2009-4645-b651-dfbd5ebb6a4a" label="text-like">taken from the ordinary Ofice for the Dead. p. 1782.</l><l xml:id="m-2fe5185f-008d-400c-bcd5-7dea2b5cfb33" facs="#m-2b0801a7-508c-434e-bcfb-e43c7443bef8" label="text-like">The Lessons of the three Nocturns are said without Absolution or</l><l xml:id="m-a228beb2-4f8d-42fd-ae47-0a6b36f95fb3" facs="#m-b7d38e1e-9d44-4e5f-9e80-5ed9ebde12ae" label="text-like">Blessing; those of the first Nocturn without any introductory title. Tu autem.</l><l xml:id="m-4f8a53bd-883b-4083-b938-32caf5faadfe" facs="#m-defbbd9c-357d-46b9-9473-e62aeced5ace" label="text-like">is not said at the end.</l><l xml:id="m-768855cd-c566-4f27-b03e-046f251da69f" facs="#m-8d925d31-627d-4986-98e2-3823857cb4d5" label="text-like">IN THE FIRST NOCTURN.</l><l xml:id="m-dcadc719-ebe3-4423-aa05-034bfc001e93" facs="#m-0a686284-8761-4229-8818-3618b2c47118" label="ambiguous">Job 7, 16-21.</l><l xml:id="m-486f6dc5-dc93-4c06-a248-1d0eb0ddaf48" facs="#m-d4fe0a3a-40af-434a-be42-6318ffe5bd60" label="ambiguous">Lesson I.</l><l xml:id="m-d27a7031-1c36-475a-9a51-c572070f9222" facs="#m-7ed4e29a-7083-4760-8a50-5b3a3356c092" label="lyrics-like">DArce mihi, Dómine; nihil enim ¡o custos hóminum? quare posuísti</l><l xml:id="m-d7ecc7b4-c165-4c76-8331-e40282679563" facs="#m-89e3c331-435c-4dda-9e00-3a3871ae21d0" label="lyrics-like">E sunt dies mei. Quid est homo, ] me contrárium tibi, et factus sum</l><l xml:id="m-5b867130-6da7-4f0a-b451-7278e1174eb2" facs="#m-4d2a58ce-4cea-48e8-844e-2dea2fd92568" label="lyrics-like">quia magníficas eum? aut quid</l><l xml:id="m-bd60ad6e-72e9-4d03-9dcf-9104f68e68b2" facs="#m-f3d68e88-7d1a-4486-8a02-39eaa499a7cc" label="ambiguous">mihimetipsi gravis? Cur non tollis</l><l xml:id="m-fd261852-6974-4942-ae97-ca461680a33c" facs="#m-e625a8db-19eb-4af7-b5c7-3d8c2a49c82d" label="lyrics-like">appónis erga eum cor tuum? Visi¬</l><l xml:id="m-1cda164d-3875-4350-8175-defff0663cd1" facs="#m-7f3d6c2b-3690-4dca-8c34-161a1f06b6cb" label="lyrics-like">peccátum meum, et quare non au¬</l><l xml:id="m-896ef67e-2d2b-49bf-b874-99775c572d0e" facs="#m-581d1711-0222-404e-b277-6f1e885e26a0" label="lyrics-like">tas eum dilúculo, et súbito probas</l><l xml:id="m-633e1d45-f8e2-47e9-b6a1-6024b04b038b" facs="#m-25b3b855-a49a-4afa-a6c9-bc59991e7ca5" label="lyrics-like">fers iniquitátem meam? ecce nunc</l><l xml:id="m-678b128b-8867-42f9-a96c-8283cdf31f12" facs="#m-86512b4f-83e5-4ef6-b5c1-5154279c9c12" label="ambiguous">illum. Usquequo non parcis mihi,</l><l xml:id="m-ec6f5636-0efd-46b5-89d8-accb6f9fe441" facs="#m-b4238254-cd20-4568-8118-2ddd83dd8852" label="lyrics-like">in púlvere dórmiam: et si mane me</l><l xml:id="m-e9155724-6342-48a9-980b-155fda93a985" facs="#m-b6764f79-02b2-4cc1-8eaf-ad081c7355e9" label="lyrics-like">nec dimittis me, ut glútiam salivam</l><l xml:id="m-43656d78-581f-4372-87cc-f2ae467acfcd" facs="#m-33d1512d-bd4c-45e0-b279-ca00f96a17a0" label="lyrics-like">quaesíeris, non subsístam.</l><l xml:id="m-fa4d8ad5-10d1-4681-92a5-22fc182cc6dc" facs="#m-9a2f7937-0ddc-4b34-87e0-47c6bbd2a160" label="lyrics-like">meam? Peccávi, quid fáciam tibi,</l><l xml:id="m-10b93aed-55ac-4113-8e2c-473f957a368d" facs="#m-57967d38-d89c-42e2-ac21-afa3f809bc75" label="lyrics-like">R. Crédo. D. 1785.</l><l xml:id="m-d659e225-9a7d-4f85-9da2-625a5c85d554" facs="#m-d6ae3587-6a5b-403f-8aa1-fe17c057c389" label="ambiguous">Lesson II.</l><l xml:id="m-c0b79ab6-0e20-4720-89bb-4278d9def960" facs="#m-16d47fbe-6ad7-497c-a40f-cc2a193dcd5a" label="ambiguous">Job 14. 146.</l><l xml:id="m-ff453dd0-0b1d-4af2-b873-3cbc19a2d086" facs="#m-5ea8e475-5a9c-40f3-a531-2c0bd0bb9559" label="ambiguous">zOmo natus de muliere, brevi vi-net. Et dignum ducis super huius¬</l><l xml:id="m-c69b0724-0c2e-47bf-9ea2-573c02283af4" facs="#m-232c566b-7c12-4127-93d8-67007c2407e0" label="lyrics-like">Lt vens témpore, replétur multis</l><l xml:id="m-33fd44b5-5ac4-4dd5-a5db-33b86841b204" facs="#m-fe0cf4ae-6471-4bbf-bb45-fdfcc7f57b7a" label="lyrics-like">cémodi aperire óculos tuos, et ad¬</l><l xml:id="m-183cc1ec-4e42-42cd-8290-931e56ac86da" facs="#m-233d0314-2977-4e91-b1e0-198a5fef9a63" label="lyrics-like">misériis. Qui quasi flos egréditur et</l><l xml:id="m-4a681beb-3e80-44a9-9383-e3acaf3b4f5e" facs="#m-7e617140-d73c-468a-b5d8-6e4c8d407a23" label="lyrics-like">dúcere eum tecum in iudícium?</l><l xml:id="m-a2295e74-b763-402d-88bc-76969f4ed6c9" facs="#m-584e188b-0057-45e7-bbc3-6b1e0e16f911" label="lyrics-like">contéritur, et fugit velut umbra, et Quis potest fácere mundum de im¬</l><l xml:id="m-d09e0656-d193-41a6-9dde-27123f9a9689" facs="#m-11953a97-4205-48e6-b38f-ced35d7c5fe7" label="lyrics-like">numquam in eódem statu pérma- múndo concéptum sémine? Nonne</l></lg></div></section></score></mdiv></body></music>
</mei>